title='Evaluating Deep Reinforcement Learning for Traffic Signal Control Under Real Toronto Demand'

sections=[
('METHOD',[
('Data and split.', 'The implemented loader selects TCS 379, Eglinton Avenue East / Danforth Road, from Toronto\'s turning-movement counts [1]. Cars, trucks, and buses retain their recorded movements; pedestrian fields identify the leg being crossed. Counts are validated and reproduced by 15-minute interval. Before controller experiments, record identifiers and file hashes were saved. Table I gives the frozen partition. The original June afternoon training period was divided into a two-hour train interval and a one-hour dev interval. Both proposed test periods remain reserved: only demand totals were audited, not controller performance. No test routes or scores were generated by the learning pipeline.'),
('Simulator and baseline.', 'SUMO 1.28.0 uses a georeferenced OpenStreetMap road extract [2], with lane assignments and movement connections adapted for this isolated junction. It includes sidewalks, four full-width signalized crossings, and separate eastern carriageways. Lane widths, corner radii, sidewalk dimensions, the 2.4 m eastern median, transit operations, and historical 2024 fidelity remain uncalibrated. The fixed-time baseline uses a simplified interpretation of the published TCS 379 PM card [3]: advance green/yellow/red of 7/3/1 s, EW WALK/clearance of 31/22 s, yellow/red of 4/3 s, NS WALK/clearance of 8/34 s, then yellow/red of 4/3 s. Total cycle length is 120 s; detector calls are not reproduced.'),
('Demand realization.', 'Exactly the observed vehicle and pedestrian totals are generated. Arrivals are uniform within each observed interval; pedestrian directions are approximately balanced because directional counts are absent. Walk speed is fixed at 1.2 m/s, with trip endpoints 0.5 m from the junction. These are explicit assumptions, not measured trajectories. Each episode starts empty, has no warm-up, and permits up to 3,600 s of drainage after arrivals end. Controllers share the same geometry and seeded arrival realizations. Pending vehicle entry is retained in the delay accounting.'),
('Learning environment.', 'Stable-Baselines3 DQN and PPO [4] use a custom Gymnasium adapter with the TraCI-compatible libsumo API [5]. The installed SUMO-RL default phase builder does not retain this complete clearance sequence, so its phase-switching controller is not used. One action per cycle selects EW WALK from {7, 19, 25, 31, 32} s; NS WALK receives the remainder of 39 s. Both WALK periods remain at least 7 s. All other intervals and the phase order are immutable. The observation contains per-leg vehicle counts, queues, pending insertions, waiting pedestrians, maximum pedestrian wait, and the previous action. Scaling is fixed; no statistics are fitted on dev.'),
('Reward and training.', 'The reward is the negative integral of approach vehicle queues, vehicles awaiting insertion, and stopped pedestrians, with equal road-user weights. It is sampled every 5 s and divided by 1,200 per cycle; unfinished demand receives an additional terminal penalty. Each algorithm was trained for 2,048 cycle decisions for seeds 101, 202, and 303, using only train demand. Each used a 64-by-64 MLP, learning rate 0.0003, discount 0.99, and batch size 64. DQN used a 20,000-entry replay buffer, 180-decision learning start, and final exploration 0.05. PPO used 256-step rollouts and 10 epochs. Full settings were recorded before learning. One preset configuration per algorithm and one documented fixed plan were evaluated; no hyperparameter search was performed.'),
('Metrics and hardware.', 'Vehicle timeLoss measures loss relative to ideal travel speed; departDelay measures waiting before insertion [6]. Their sum is reported as a vehicle delay proxy, alongside the two components. Pedestrian walk timeLoss is reported separately. These simulation proxies are not field-calibrated intersection delay. Completion, collisions, teleports, and emergency braking are retained; incomplete demand would invalidate an all-demand delay ranking. Runs used Windows, Python '+env['python']+', an Intel Family 6 Model 154 CPU with 20 logical processors, PyTorch 2.15.0+cpu, and libsumo 1.28.0. No GPU was used.'),
]),
('FIRST EXPERIMENTS',[
('Baseline and checks.', 'The data loader and fixed-time simulation run end to end. Across five dev demand seeds (11, 22, 33, 44, 55), mean vehicle time loss was 55.12 +/- 3.72 s/vehicle and departure delay was 111.09 +/- 9.22 s/vehicle. Combined delay was 166.21 +/- 10.16 s/vehicle, while pedestrian time loss was 46.93 +/- 1.43 s/person. Values are mean +/- sample SD. All 3,594 vehicles and 518 pedestrians finished in each run. The new adapter reproduced the saved baseline exactly. A 600-state action audit checked every legal allocation, and a 7,200-state trace checked 60 fixed cycles and all intended pedestrian crossings.'),
('Pilot comparison.', 'Each last checkpoint was evaluated deterministically on the same five dev realizations: 15 cases per RL algorithm and five fixed-time cases. Table II gives case means; Table III reports policy-seed variation. DQN selected the baseline 31/8 allocation for every dev cycle across all three trained policies and therefore reproduced its results exactly. PPO was unstable across training seeds: its vehicle-proxy means were 253.89, 227.53, and 152.52 s/vehicle. Its average was worse than fixed-time. The favorable seed is not selected as proof of improvement. This initial pilot does not establish a DRL benefit.'),
('Uncertainty and limits.', 'A paired, two-way bootstrap resampled three policy seeds and five shared demand seeds (4,000 samples; random seed 5420). PPO minus fixed-time combined vehicle delay was +45.11 s, with exploratory 95% interval [-12.28, 87.64] s. The pedestrian difference was -0.32 s, interval [-0.92, 0.24] s. Both span zero; small improvements are not established. DQN differences are identically zero because its actions match the baseline. No collisions or teleports occurred in the 35 dev cases; emergency braking averaged 1.2, 1.2, and 2.0 events per case for fixed-time, DQN, and PPO. Repeated stochastic episodes do not add independent observed days. Time-blocked cross-validation has not yet been performed.'),
]),
('EVIDENCE, ISSUES, AND REVISED PLAN',[
('Reproducibility and hosted evidence.', 'The local repository contains the loader, frozen row identifiers and hashes, model, control adapter, six trained checkpoints, per-seed metrics, and configuration. The experiment is under experiments/pilot_v1; its dev_summary.json is the numerical source for this report. W&B recorded six training runs with learning histories and model artifacts, plus a matched-dev comparison. These are offline runs indexed by wandb_runs.json. <b>Hosted repository URL: not yet created. Hosted W&B URLs: not yet synchronized.</b> Account sign-in and publication remain required to satisfy the evidence-link checklist; local artifacts are not presented as hosted links.'),
('Problems found and corrected.', 'Runtime tracing exposed a guessed crossing that let 62 south-leg pedestrians bypass the signal; that shortcut was removed and all 518 dev pedestrians were verified on the correct legs. A preliminary training attempt failed because a diagnostic and training process shared a temporary statistics file. That attempt was archived and excluded; all successful models restarted after process-specific output isolation. These issues and the null/unstable learning result are retained as evidence rather than hidden.'),
('Revised scope.', 'The check-in now has a running baseline and a bounded pilot; further training is not required to make this report concrete. Next, publish the repository and synchronize the existing W&B runs, then insert verified links. A later development experiment should inspect PPO\'s green allocations and entry queues, consider a separately tuned fixed-allocation diagnostic with comparable dev tuning effort, and revise training budget/reward only through dev. Field calibration and time-blocked validation remain necessary before broad claims. Test periods stay sealed until the final configuration is frozen; changing a model after viewing test performance would require relabeling that test as dev.'),
]),
]
refs=[
'[1] City of Toronto, "Traffic volumes - multimodal intersection turning movement counts," Toronto Open Data. <link href="https://open.toronto.ca/dataset/traffic-volumes-at-intersections-for-all-modes/" color="blue">Dataset and dictionary</link>, accessed Nov. 11, 2026.',
'[2] OpenStreetMap contributors, "Eglinton Avenue East / Danforth Road map extract," ODbL 1.0, downloaded Nov. 9, 2026. <link href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" color="blue">Attribution and licence</link>.',
'[3] City of Toronto, "Current Signal Timing Information: TCS 379," Oct. 31, 2019, in WSP, 320 McCowan Road Transportation Impact Study, Feb. 14, 2020, App. B, PDF p. 147. <link href="https://320mccowan.ca/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/TransportationReport_320McCowan.pdf" color="blue">Source report</link>.',
'[4] Stable-Baselines3, "Using custom environments," v. 2.9.2 documentation. <link href="https://stable-baselines3.readthedocs.io/en/master/guide/custom_env.html" color="blue">Documentation</link>, accessed Nov. 11, 2026.',
'[5] Eclipse SUMO, "Libsumo." <link href="https://sumo.dlr.de/docs/Libsumo.html" color="blue">Documentation</link>, accessed Nov. 11, 2026.',
'[6] Eclipse SUMO, "TripInfo." <link href="https://sumo.dlr.de/docs/Simulation/Output/TripInfo.html" color="blue">Metric definitions</link>, accessed Nov. 11, 2026.',
]
tables={}
tables['Data and split.']=('I','FROZEN OBSERVED DEMAND PARTITIONS (2024)',[
    ['Set / date / period','Rows','Veh.','Peds'],
    ['Train: Jun. 19, 15-17',8,'6,716',810],['Dev: Jun. 19, 17-18',4,'3,594',518],
    ['Test: Nov. 2, 15-18',12,'9,961','1,598'],['Test: Jun. 19, 07-10',12,'8,275',661]], [134,30,44,44])
tables['Pilot comparison.']=('II','DEV CASE MEANS (SECONDS PER ROAD USER)',[
    ['Control','Veh. loss','Entry','Combined','Ped. loss'],
    *[[a,*[f'{summary["controllers"][a]["pooled_case_metrics"][k]["mean"]:.2f}' for k in
        ['vehicle_time_loss_s','vehicle_depart_delay_s','vehicle_combined_delay_proxy_s','pedestrian_time_loss_s']]] for a in ['fixed','DQN','PPO']]], [42,49,46,65,50])
policy_table=[['Policy seed','Vehicle combined','Pedestrian loss']]
for seed,metrics in ppo['by_training_seed'].items():
    a,b=metrics['vehicle_combined_delay_proxy_s'],metrics['pedestrian_time_loss_s']
    policy_table.append([f'PPO {seed}',f'{a["mean"]:.2f} +/- {a["sample_std_across_demand"]:.2f}',f'{b["mean"]:.2f} +/- {b["sample_std_across_demand"]:.2f}'])
policy_table.append(['DQN: all 3','166.21 +/- 10.16','46.93 +/- 1.43'])
tables['Uncertainty and limits.']=('III','EACH POLICY: FIVE DEMAND SEEDS, MEAN +/- SD',policy_table,[66,95,91])

body=ParagraphStyle('body',fontName='Times-Roman',fontSize=10,leading=11.5,alignment=TA_JUSTIFY,spaceAfter=5)
small=ParagraphStyle('small',parent=body,fontSize=8,leading=9.2,alignment=0,spaceAfter=3)
heading=ParagraphStyle('heading',parent=body,alignment=TA_CENTER,spaceBefore=7,spaceAfter=6,keepWithNext=True)
caption=ParagraphStyle('caption',parent=small,alignment=TA_CENTER,spaceBefore=5,spaceAfter=5,keepWithNext=True)
story=[]
abstract='This check-in reports an implemented multimodal SUMO baseline, a frozen train/dev/test split, and a bounded DQN/PPO pilot. Fixed-time dev vehicle delay proxy is 166.21 +/- 10.16 s/vehicle. DQN reproduces the baseline; PPO is unstable and worse on average. No robust DRL benefit is established. Hosted evidence links remain a submission dependency.'
story.append(Paragraph('<b>Abstract</b> - '+abstract,body))

def make_table(data,widths):
    obj=Table([[Paragraph(str(c),small) for c in row] for row in data],colWidths=widths,hAlign='CENTER')
    obj.setStyle(TableStyle([('LINEABOVE',(0,0),(-1,0),.6,colors.black),('LINEBELOW',(0,0),(-1,0),.4,colors.black),('LINEBELOW',(0,-1),(-1,-1),.6,colors.black),('VALIGN',(0,0),(-1,-1),'TOP'),('LEFTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),3),('RIGHTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),3),('TOPPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),3),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),2)]))
    return obj

for number,(section,paragraphs) in enumerate(sections,1):
    story.append(Paragraph(['I','II','III'][number-1]+'. '+section,heading))
    for lead,text in paragraphs:
        story.append(Paragraph('<i>'+lead+'</i> '+text,body))
        if lead in tables:
            n,cap,data,widths=tables[lead]
            story.append(Paragraph('TABLE '+n+'<br/>'+cap,caption))
            story.append(make_table(data,widths))
            story.append(Spacer(1,5))
story.append(Paragraph('REFERENCES',heading))
story.extend(Paragraph(r,small) for r in refs)

W,H=8.5*inch,11*inch
left,bottom,col,gap=45,54,252,18
def footer(canvas,doc):
    canvas.setFont('Times-Roman',8)
    canvas.drawCentredString(W/2,32,str(doc.page))
def first(canvas,doc):
    p=Paragraph(title,ParagraphStyle('title',fontName='Times-Roman',fontSize=22,leading=24,alignment=TA_CENTER))
    _,height=p.wrap(W-90,120)
    p.drawOn(canvas,left,H-48-height)
    y=H-48-height-22
    for text in ['Jowel Akkeh','Department of Civil Engineering, Lassonde School of Engineering','York University, Toronto, Canada']:
        canvas.setFont('Times-Roman',10);canvas.drawCentredString(W/2,y,text);y-=12
    canvas.setFont('Times-Italic',9)
    canvas.drawCentredString(W/2,y-3,'GS/ESS 5420 - Individual check-in - November 11, 2026')
    footer(canvas,doc)
doc=BaseDocTemplate(str(OUT/'Progress_Report_Jowel_Akkeh.pdf'),pagesize=(W,H),title=title,author='Jowel Akkeh')
first_frames=[Frame(left+i*(col+gap),bottom,col,554,id=f'f{i}',leftPadding=0,rightPadding=0,topPadding=0,bottomPadding=0) for i in range(2)]
other_frames=[Frame(left+i*(col+gap),bottom,col,H-108,id=f'b{i}',leftPadding=0,rightPadding=0,topPadding=0,bottomPadding=0) for i in range(2)]
doc.addPageTemplates([PageTemplate(id='first',frames=first_frames,onPage=first,autoNextPageTemplate='body'),PageTemplate(id='body',frames=other_frames,onPage=footer)])
doc.build(story)

def plain(s):return html.unescape(re.sub('<[^>]+>','',s))
def tex(s):
    return ''.join({'&':r'\&','%':r'\%','$':r'\$','#':r'\#','_':r'\_','{':r'\{','}':r'\}'}.get(c,c) for c in plain(s)).replace('+/-',r'$\pm$')
source=[r'\documentclass[conference]{IEEEtran}',r'\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}',r'\usepackage{url}',r'\begin{document}',r'\title{'+tex(title)+'}',r'\author{\IEEEauthorblockN{Jowel Akkeh}\IEEEauthorblockA{Department of Civil Engineering, Lassonde School of Engineering\\York University, Toronto, Canada}}',r'\maketitle',r'\begin{abstract}'+tex(abstract)+r'\end{abstract}']
markdown=['# '+title,'','Jowel Akkeh - GS/ESS 5420 - November 11, 2026','',abstract]
for section,paragraphs in sections:
    source.append(r'\section{'+tex(section)+'}')
    markdown+=['','## '+section]
    for lead,text in paragraphs:
        source.append(r'\paragraph{'+tex(lead.rstrip('.'))+'} '+tex(text))
        markdown+=['','**'+lead+'** '+plain(text)]
        if lead in tables:
            number,cap,data,_=tables[lead]
            source += [r'\begin{table}[ht]\centering\footnotesize',r'\caption{'+tex(cap)+'}',r'\begin{tabular}{'+('l'+'r'*(len(data[0])-1))+r'}\hline']
            source += [' & '.join(tex(str(c)) for c in row)+r' \\' for row in data]
            source += [r'\hline\end{tabular}\end{table}']
            markdown+=['','Table '+number+': '+cap,'','| '+' | '.join(str(c) for c in data[0])+' |','| '+' | '.join('---' for c in data[0])+' |']
            markdown += ['| '+' | '.join(str(c) for c in row)+' |' for row in data[1:]]
source.append(r'\begin{thebibliography}{6}')
for i,r in enumerate(refs,1):
    source.append(r'\bibitem{r'+str(i)+'} '+tex(re.sub(r'^\[\d+\] ','',r)))
source += [r'\end{thebibliography}',r'\end{document}']
(OUT/'main.tex').write_text('\n'.join(source),encoding='utf-8')
(OUT/'Progress_Report_Editable.md').write_text('\n'.join(markdown),encoding='utf-8')
print(OUT/'Progress_Report_Jowel_Akkeh.pdf')
